Task: AsyncApiSpecWriter (Phase 1, Tasks 3-4 of sbt-asyncapi-plugin_20261017)

Summary: Added AsyncApiSpecWriter.main(providerClass, title, version,
outputPath) - reflectively loads a consuming service's AsyncApiChannelsProvider
singleton by class name, generates its AsyncAPI document via the existing
AsyncApiDoc.generate, and writes the JSON to disk via plain java.nio.file
(no new dependency). This is the entry point the sbt plugin's
asyncApiGenerateSpec task (Phase 3) will invoke via Compile/runMain in the
consuming service's own JVM.

Files:
- modules/purekafka/src/main/scala/purekafka/docs/AsyncApiSpecWriter.scala (new)
- modules/purekafka/src/test/scala/purekafka/docs/AsyncApiSpecWriterSuite.scala (new)

Why: Replaces the shell-script-based spec generation step with a pure-Scala
one the sbt plugin can run directly, no Node toolchain needed for the JSON
half (Node is only needed later, in Phase 4, for the HTML rendering step).

Applied the $-suffix reflection fix documented on commit 71eaeb4's git note
directly (Class.forName(providerClass + "$")) rather than rediscovering it.

TDD: Red confirmed via `sbt "pureKafka/testOnly purekafka.docs.AsyncApiSpecWriterSuite"`
(compile failure: "Not found: AsyncApiSpecWriter"), then Green after
implementing the writer. Full `pureKafka/test` suite (36 tests) passes.
scalafmtCheck on the two new files is clean; pre-existing formatting drift
